    "created_at": "2020-01-08T19:47:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-08T19:47:43Z",
    "body": "Doh, thanks for catching this @paigr. The problem is slightly different to what you noticed, basically what the module does is just loops through every file for the `current_context` if it finds it it then looks for the namespace in the same file. The problem as you have noticed is that the `current_context` when changed is only set in the first file which while the namespace might be found in a different file.\r\n\r\nI think the solution would be to split the function that gets the context and the function that gets the namespace, so we loop over the files looking for the context then go back a loop over looking for the namespace. I'll try to get a PR to fix this later this week if I have time or feel free to have a go yourself if you know rust. ",
